Statistic, 1 = Value. Mean, 1 = 0.049. Median, 1 = 0.016. Standard Deviation, 1 = 0.087. 95th Percentile, 1 = 0.215. 99th Percentile, 1 = 0.438
Figure 9: Distribution of similarity scores across all cell type pairs, with a logarithmic frequency scale.

SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE

Histogram plot showing the distribution of similarity values. The x-axis is labeled “Similarity Score” and ranges from about 0.0 to 1.0. The y-axis is labeled “Frequency (log scale)” with logarithmic tick marks. The plot title is “Distribution of Similarity Values.”

The bars are highest near similarity score 0 and decrease steadily as similarity increases, indicating many low-similarity pairs and progressively fewer high-similarity pairs. There is also a distinct spike at or near 1.0, suggesting a smaller set of identical or nearly identical comparisons.
Figure 10: Cumulative distribution of similarity scores.

SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE

Line plot showing a cumulative distribution of similarity values. The x-axis is labeled “Similarity Score” and ranges from about 0 to 1; the y-axis is labeled “Cumulative Probability” and ranges from 0 to 1. The title is “Cumulative Distribution of Similarity Values.” A single blue curve rises steeply near similarity score 0, reaches roughly 0.9 cumulative probability by around 0.15, and approaches 1.0 by about 0.5, indicating most similarity scores are low with a long tail toward higher similarity.
